Groove MIDI Dataset

The drum classifier of Convert to MIDI (Drums), the coefficients in
ReBuzz/Core/AudioLibrary/AudioToMidi/DrumModelData.cs, was FITTED ON this dataset:
the train and validation splits of the Groove MIDI Dataset v1.0.0.

  Title:    The Groove MIDI Dataset
  Authors:  Jon Gillick, Adam Roberts, Jesse Engel, Douglas Eck and David Bamman
            (Magenta, Google; University of California, Berkeley)
  Paper:    Learning to Groove with Inverse Sequence Transformations,
            International Conference on Machine Learning (ICML), 2019
  Source:   https://magenta.tensorflow.org/datasets/groove
  Licence:  Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
            https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Changes: the dataset's recordings were analysed (band energies around each drum hit)
and a small neural network was fitted to tell the drums apart; only that network's
coefficients (a few thousand numbers, no audio and no MIDI of the dataset) are part of
this software. The test split of the dataset was not used for fitting; it is used only
to measure the result. The dataset's authors do not endorse this software.

The training also used synthetic drum loops generated by this repository's own test
signals; no other recordings were used to fit the coefficients. The sets this software
is only measured on (IDMT-SMT-Drums, MDB Drums) are not part of it.
